decision: changes-requested

Three medium blockers remain in ADR association parsing:

- **N50, line 37:** valid reference definitions with multiline labels, escaped brackets, or blockquote prefixes disappear silently.
- **N51, line 35:** valid angle-bracket links containing an escaped `>` can disappear silently.
- **N52, line 56:** entity decoding incorrectly interprets backslash-escaped character references.

Each can grant an incorrect `when-justified` exemption. Read-only probes compared the extracted production expressions with CommonMark rendering. These forms are supported by the [CommonMark specification](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#links).

The closeout-policy tests passed across domain, CLI, and MCP packages; `go vet ./...` passed. Surface-check reported zero findings. The exact artifact-check exited 0, with provenance warnings and an older recorded change set; an additional explicit-range invocation failed with `signal: broken pipe`.

Rules applied: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence under the review workflow. No repository changes or attestation were made.

